From a4f63a687bca6b3edcafe7e4f39739003aa79c0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <agent@cursor.local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:17:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(android): always startForeground for torrent service,
 stop relying on activeNotifications
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ServiceNotification decided whether to call startForeground() and whether to refresh
the notification by looking up its own id in NotificationManager.activeNotifications.
That assumption breaks on Android compatibility layers (HarmonyOS 卓易通) where the
shade is bridged to the host OS: a stale notification made the service skip
startForeground() and run as a plain background service (frozen on background/lock
screen), and a missing entry made every notification update a silent no-op, so the
'downloading N resources' state never showed up.

- Always call startForeground() (idempotent) and track foreground state locally.
- Keep the last display strategy so restarts do not reset the notification to idle.
- Catch IllegalStateException/SecurityException with stack traces; warn when
  notifications or the channel are blocked so bug reports show it.
- AniTorrentService stops itself when the foreground start is refused.
- AniTorrentServiceStarter times out (15s) waiting for the startup broadcast instead
  of hanging forever.
